# c3: integrations/
seg-27636d757dba = <b>The native OpenCPN plugin</b> (<c1/>) is licensed <b>GPL-3.0-or-later</b> (see the <c2/> file in that directory), not AGPL-3.0, and is <b>not</b> offered under the commercial licence. It is loaded into OpenCPN and built against its GPL-2.0-or-later plugin API header, which is the usual basis for OpenCPN plugins. The rest of <c3/> (the Signal K plugin and the OpenCPN TCP relay) stays AGPL-3.0-only.

# text
seg-f90c983e0ee3 = <b>Kshana Pro</b> and other proprietary overlays are <b>separate, closed-source</b> products under their own commercial terms. They are not part of this repository and are not offered under the AGPL.

# text
# c1: deny.toml
seg-e340445b7f17 = <b>Dependencies</b> keep their own (permissive) licences. We deliberately keep the dependency tree permissive (Apache-2.0 / MIT / BSD / ISC / …) precisely so the commercial edition can be offered cleanly — a copyleft dependency would taint it. See <a1><c1/></a1>.

