seg-810191f19d4d = <b>Galileo E1 primary memory codes</b> (<c1/>, <c2/>; <b>not bundled since { "0.36" }</b>: each user supplies their own copy, <c3/> or <c4/> / <c5/>, read by <c6/>). These are the E1-B and E1-C primary codes of Annex C.7 and C.8 of the Galileo Open Service Signal-In-Space Interface Control Document (OS SIS ICD), Issue { "2.0" }, January { "2021" }, © European Union { "2021" }, extracted unmodified from the PDF's attachments (source URL, SHA-256 and a cross-check against Issue { "1.3" } are in <a1><c7/></a1>). They are <b>not</b> covered by the AGPL-3.0 or the commercial licence, and neither licence grants anything over them. What the ICD itself says, quoted from Issue { "2.0" }:

# text
seg-daef032cbe43 = Terms of Use §{ "3" }: "The information contained in the OS SIS ICD, including its Annexes, is subject to intellectual property rights". "The OS SIS ICD may only be partly or wholly reproduced and/or transmitted to a third party in accordance with the herein described permitted use and under the following conditions: the present “Terms of Use and Disclaimers”, as well as the terms of Annex G, are accepted, reproduced and transmitted entirely and unmodified together with the reproduced and/or transmitted information; the copyright notice “© European Union { "2021" }” is not removed from any page." And: "The use of the information contained in the OS SIS ICD, including the spreading codes which are subject to IPR, is authorised under the terms and conditions stated in Annex G."

# text
seg-0fb25fafd9a2 = Annex G (Issue { "2.0" }; Annex H in Issue { "2.1" }, same wording) defines "Technical Data of the OS SIS ICD" to include the "E1 and E5 Memory Codes", and grants a covenant not to assert that is "non-exclusive and royalty-free" and "non-transferable and non-licensable". Its §G.3 list, which it calls exhaustive, covers: "a) the use of the Technical Data of the OS SIS ICD, including their integration and incorporation into any Products"; "b) the storage of the Technical Data of the OS SIS ICD, provided the source is acknowledged"; "c) the reproduction of the OS SIS ICD, in whole or in part, its distribution and its publication for non-commercial not-for-profit purposes and scale without amending the document or adding any element"; and "d) providing links to the EU website where the document is published". "Products" means software, devices and value-added services "making use of the OS Signal". It also says: "The Authorised Person shall not state or imply in any promotional material or elsewhere that the Products were developed by, are used by or for or have been approved or endorsed by the EU".

# text
seg-8531368368ba = <b>Decision ({ "0.36" }): not redistributed.</b> No explicit open licence is stated. Use inside a software product (G.3 a) and storage with the source acknowledged (G.3 b) are covered on the ICD's own terms, but redistribution (G.3 c) only for non-commercial, not-for-profit purposes and with the Terms and Annex G reproduced unmodified alongside. Because Kshana is also offered under a commercial licence, the files were removed from the repository and its packages; the engine reads the user's own copy at run time, and without it the Galileo E1 signals return an error that says how to supply them. Each user relies on the EU's Authorisation directly; Kshana cannot pass it on. Kshana is not developed by, used by, approved by or endorsed by the European Union.

